 | ![](images/65/6559bd5ce9529a5fb62118898302bc3b3e6acca3dcaf0d4ada238952f002b3e0.png) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ![](images/9d/9dd38e65c9ac4ac71d8e33eb17be8154c0cff0da1da5c66ebbf213b8a4d36fff.png) | ![](images/39/39795cdf5281bb4e22ea8ab0d66ac72811d1eafc079f1df3d376c7483a025a55.png) | ![](images/08/087d931b3bc72d994c664730dcf2602fa23e373cf5c53208e0ab0f33b2088e03.png) | ![](images/2c/2c7813255732725f637dbaa1e776b38fd33b2b0a8294c5c36e9a6151eb44c424.png) | ![](images/55/558b2c5a57371dfadac033aa8427f91f4c2e5b1e4b69e9a4a31b2fdf57c0a6df.png) |\n| ![](images/2a/2aa90d03b55f4e82c1cb4d5458005fcb389035bceb6438fb3209a30660811c8c.png) | ![](images/07/078d78866a2b1230a92b3ddcd5e7b9dac37590dc890403f8e8a4946675c2c4d6.png) | ![](images/8f/8f83a4788c972a5b0808b8227f77c667f5fb05101cc0ee4676fa5caa685dde6a.png) | ![](images/af/af9a43f2c0971b0aa4889ebbae1c6e962234cc0a1a3cdcb1e6894d4696b57e47.png) | ![](images/f6/f6938e51455223b87c100bb473ef1485d4dcd077074caf699c2869ac160933a9.png) |\n| ![](images/e0/e08652bada58ecdbec6c7fdd3a4a8d547bb7e0b97f882937341b3caf5bf0ded6.png) | ![](images/6f/6fe8b651d3f16e4d0f29576d66fdee089782d80678f2c47e3a567bc49e7512b0.png) | ![](images/2f/2f797f3faf0840f0680cb070cb6c2e4e9e532e4afd808edc26c51e01987524ef.png) | ![](images/f9/f90bfc1980145c9481dd78c946a51ba5b5966ee25f374f50e44338e36dd39b3a.png) | ![](images/81/810d69a3fdd768331ea9e5d0f6bcb832615c64be87d6b1208da59a095a8db23d.png) |\n| ![](images/72/72597034419790c36dcb627c6235264c675e2ad82b3dc466b026d95c304761e5.png) | ![](images/53/5338f819663df9f3d5a240f2f71238f34315bd5e94e23842bb5c76e506219134.png) | ![](images/91/91bdf45a377b9dea772b0b450bc9d15ba9eb42d8ed83e98761486ae3ab607b4d.png) | ![](images/7a/7a83cc1918ba2b00f80be5d4c5b1209f296875d839412ebc49906aee5fd28448.png) | ![](images/2a/2a04324d390f3a0c7f333aef876bd58403443dabe51f572e98601d4f09f0c9fb.png) |\n\nTherefore, for ![](images/74/740061c94d617bd1251e7dd3578cd4bfbf60bf0d9071f55a3e3a7d847fc2506a.png) we obtain the following:\n\n![](images/2a/2ac45605d166c1d5e62e00ead41197afa81b350bc55f2c9bf3f55c3ef585a475.png)\n\nFinally, the conditional probability mass function can be represented by the following table:   \n\n| ![](images/85/85762ec9b76821c157ddf5309b6a086ff5f92f0ddf5fcfe4862387b07ccba0f0.png) | ![](images/70/70a98018f2f0a36bda308aaf3137678bf6ddf46f69db2a391f6918687f9d647e.png) | ![](images/d4/d4db3ce76156bd8fe5bc5201404c2dbd5ae7e0a0bbb11c29bc4592bee357a619.png) | ![](images/0f/0fb592e51276f95b696a525503d7f39fbfbe16ca98468ebad9c288fd211f371c.png) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ![](images/95/954ead5794558eeeae70337a0dcddbaf3784e6d50dbf92aa898476f4270a63f8.png) | ![](images/59/595c03f7164ad392f4a99bec5c2df94de089f3ae01f28940ec2f42c358f054af.png) | ![](images/06/06490ba8fc0d09765bc33d63d8db345c702d6f01a7f37ef757e6b92af97e3363.png) | ![](images/59/595c03f7164ad392f4a99bec5c2df94de089f3ae01f28940ec2f42c358f054af.png) |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161671 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162105 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "277b8807-fb74-5ad3-a89b-92dbf90bc075" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Value of a Conditional Probability Mass Function at a Point"}] :question/id #uuid "0e42cf0f-f1bd-5762-a4fc-3cedec697c14" :question/math-academy-id "e-10050" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{18}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{18}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{18}$ |\n\nCompute $f_{X|Y}(2 \\,|\\, 2)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional probability mass function $f_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) = P(X = x \\,|\\, Y=y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the conditional probability\n\n$$\nf_{X|Y}(2 \\,|\\, 2) = P(X = 2 \\,|\\, Y = 2).\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(X = 2 \\,|\\, Y = 2) = \\dfrac{P(X = 2, Y = 2)}{P(Y = 2)} = \\dfrac{f(2,2)}{f_Y(2)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and $f_Y(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(2) & =f(1,2)+f(2,2)+f(3,2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, $f(2,2) = \\dfrac{1}{6}.$ \n\nFinally, substituting  $f_Y(2) = \\dfrac{7}{18}$ and $f(2,2) = \\dfrac{1}{6}$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(2\\,|\\,2) & =P(X=2\\,|\\,Y=2) \\\\  & =\\frac{f(2,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{6})}{(\\frac{7}{18})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161876 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162076 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87675618-337f-5af2-8ad7-9132c080785a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability"}] :question/id #uuid "ddfe8dda-9ab2-5b11-af30-159a7bd32d64" :question/math-academy-id "e-9256" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.5$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nCompute $P(Y=0 \\,|\\, X=1)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required probability is given by\n\n$$\nP(Y = 0 \\,|\\, X = 1) = \\dfrac{P(X = 1 , Y = 0)}{P(X = 1)} =  \\dfrac{f(1,0)}{f_X(1)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and $f_X(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(1) & =f(1,0)+f(1,1) \\\\  & =0.15+0.3 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(1,0) = 0.15.$ \n\nFinally, substituting $f_X(1) = 0.45$ and $f(1,0) = 0.15$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=0\\,|\\,X=1) & =\\frac{f(1,0)}{{f}_{X}(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.15}{0.45} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161877 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "348dfcb8-2325-5929-b622-5423b7e37a53" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability Over an Interval"}] :question/id #uuid "531b9a19-e424-59e5-8c02-7bca4f67e110" :question/math-academy-id "e-9258" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.2$ | $0$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ | $0$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCompute $P(0\\lt Y \\lt 3\\,|\\, X=0  )$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<Y<3\\,|\\,X=0) & =\\frac{P((0<Y<3),X=0)}{P(X=0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=0,(0<Y<3))}{P(X=0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=0,Y=1)+P(X=0,Y=2)}{P(X=0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(0,1)+f(0,2)}{{f}_{X}(0)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and $f_X(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(0) & =f(0,0)+f(0,1)+f(0,2)+f(0,3) \\\\  & =0.2+0+0.05+0.1 \\\\  & =0.35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(0,1)=0$ and $f(0,2)=0.05.$ \n\nFinally, substituting our values into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<Y<3\\,|\\,X=0) & =\\frac{f(0,1)+f(0,2)}{{f}_{X}(0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+0.05}{0.35} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.05}{0.35} \\\\  & ≈0.14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162372 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162076 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87675618-337f-5af2-8ad7-9132c080785a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d076baa-16c1-5ead-8baf-b71b24793b61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159435} {:answer/id #uuid "cee24829-5b33-5cbf-988a-e9eef36f783c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159436} {:answer/id #uuid "01a41e10-e5dc-5030-993c-64c9c2d1973a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.74" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159437} {:answer/id #uuid "4dba2cd5-fb6d-5a6c-a2b0-363cd95e9ed2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159438} {:answer/id #uuid "55369d5b-546b-5bbe-a91d-535fb8fb3367" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159439}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2c8215f3-4bea-5552-8b5e-4c1c809315eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159434}] :question/id #uuid "2a22ec54-0726-5bc9-a10c-e9f017685aa3" :question/math-academy-id "q-142547" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y = 1$ | $Y = 3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X = 2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X = 4$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X = 6$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P(Y = 3 \\mid X = 2)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x, y)$ shown in the table above. Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162374 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162104 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebabf742-2b8d-5392-a077-f34e8f4bd034" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability Mass Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1f0fda1-96e3-568d-9774-fb0fb6548025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid 2)$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159447} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e88b09-2da5-5f95-9a72-171089c21505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid 2)$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $0$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159448} {:answer/id #uuid "e24f35b5-cce9-591a-937c-dc5ab4ffc29b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid 2)$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159449} {:answer/id #uuid "467fb8f6-36c1-581b-9255-ad985661016d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid 2)$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159450} {:answer/id #uuid "60d1e2bc-af54-561f-8e3e-a8d647eb38a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid 2)$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159451}] :answer-field/id #uuid "eef8539b-508b-5fa7-a6fb-1b79927d1667" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159446}] :question/id #uuid "8cfbd164-6093-5409-a707-eefa23c3aa6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-142554" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y = 0$ | $Y = 1$ | $Y = 2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X = 0$ | $0.1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $X = 1$ | $0$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X = 2$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ |\n\nFind the conditional probability mass function $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid 2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x, y)$ shown in the table above.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363280 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162105 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "277b8807-fb74-5ad3-a89b-92dbf90bc075" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Value of a Conditional Probability Mass Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "772f1af4-3e1a-5d24-b6f2-84e08728280e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363282} {:answer/id #uuid "ed679624-c3a1-592b-b00b-85dbdf0ab4f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363283} {:answer/id #uuid "65636e3f-fc1c-570a-afb9-b6e83ab76155" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.67" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363284} {:answer/id #uuid "145ae614-6fb3-5df0-adc4-a7a23c2f414d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363285} {:answer/id #uuid "e6479b1c-edbb-5852-9f86-63ee058f8c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed679624-c3a1-592b-b00b-85dbdf0ab4f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363283} :answer-field/id #uuid "945c9fdc-f2f4-578d-8093-3c96735abd64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363281}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e911b538-24df-51a8-a134-2c4a130edca5" :question/math-academy-id "q-142890" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.35$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute ${f}_{X|Y}(4\\,|\\,2)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=P(X=x\\,|\\,Y=y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the conditional probability\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(4\\,|\\,2)=P(X=4\\,|\\,Y=2).\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=4\\,|\\,Y=2)=\\frac{P(X=4,Y=2)}{P(Y=2)}=\\frac{f(4,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(2) & =f(2,2)+f(4,2) \\\\  & =0.4+0.15 \\\\  & =0.55.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, $f(4,2)=0.15.$ \n\nFinally, substituting  ${f}_{Y}(2)=0.55$ and $f(4,2)=0.15$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(4\\,|\\,2) & =P(X=4\\,|\\,Y=2) \\\\  & =\\frac{f(4,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.15}{0.55} \\\\  & ≈0.27.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363287 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162105 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "277b8807-fb74-5ad3-a89b-92dbf90bc075" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Value of a Conditional Probability Mass Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b23a91dd-7a01-54db-9c82-1cde58ce273a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363289} {:answer/id #uuid "8145968b-18ea-5743-b1bd-efc55f689163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363290} {:answer/id #uuid "57859f6d-2835-5a6a-af22-856e77c2c686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363291} {:answer/id #uuid "771f4df6-0fd2-59bd-b1c4-8a07438c5de1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363292} {:answer/id #uuid "7678ab30-3836-51cd-9e08-1245f5e719d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "771f4df6-0fd2-59bd-b1c4-8a07438c5de1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363292} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3c83bc5-8c9c-5ba3-9c2d-a22c540d169d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37840033-8bd0-59aa-a8ed-245c50ed8426" :question/math-academy-id "q-142892" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ | $\\frac{7}{20}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{9}{20}$ | $\\frac{1}{20}$ |\n\nCompute ${f}_{X|Y}(1\\,|\\,4)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=P(X=x\\,|\\,Y=y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the conditional probability\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(1\\,|\\,4)=P(X=1\\,|\\,Y=4).\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=1\\,|\\,Y=4)=\\frac{P(X=1,Y=4)}{P(Y=4)}=\\frac{f(1,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(4) & =f(1,4)+f(3,4) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{20}+\\frac{1}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, $f(1,4)=\\frac{7}{20}.$ \n\nFinally, substituting  ${f}_{Y}(4)=\\frac{2}{5}$ and $f(1,4)=\\frac{7}{20}$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(1\\,|\\,4) & =P(X=1\\,|\\,Y=4) \\\\  & =\\frac{f(1,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{7}{20})}{(\\frac{2}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
